message.content:
{
  "technical_and_design_decisions": [
    "Implement everything in Go, aligned with the Hyperledger Fabric release-2.x codebase referenced by the specification.",
    "Deliver U2-U8 as a standalone, importable Go library module ('configtx' style package) that makes no assumptions about key storage and requires no network access; callers pass all configuration and crypto material as parameters.",
    "Copy and adapt the genesisconfig types (Profile, Application, Orderer, Consortium, Policy, Capabilities) into the new package instead of importing Fabric's internal genesisconfig/viper/yaml machinery, as mandated by U2.",
    "Reuse Fabric protobuf types (common.Config/ConfigGroup/ConfigValue/ConfigPolicy, ConfigUpdate, ConfigUpdateEnvelope, cb.Block, msp.MSPConfig) via the fabric protobuf dependency rather than redefining them.",
    "Use the functional-options pattern (Option func) on library entry points for extensibility, per the U2 sketch.",
    "For U1: extend the KV read set so the endorser optionally records a hash (SHA-256) of each read value alongside key and version; the feature is gated behind a new channel capability so older networks are unaffected.",
    "For U1: committer/VSCC validation compares each recorded value hash against a hash of the local world-state value (at the recorded version) and marks the transaction invalid with a new validation code on mismatch, preventing propagation of tampered data.",
    "For U7: port configtxlator's compute_update logic (recursive read-set/write-set construction over ConfigGroups, ConfigValues and ConfigPolicies) into the library.",
    "U5 and U8 compose the U7 compute-update function (and U6 org generation for U8) instead of duplicating diff logic; the current channel config is supplied by the caller since the library has no network access.",
    "For U3/U4: use standard Fabric signing semantics (signature header carrying the serialized creator identity; ECDSA signature over the concatenation of signature header and payload bytes); detached signatures are collected into ConfigUpdateEnvelope.ConfigUpdateSignatures and wrapped in a signed common.Envelope.",
    "Verify correctness with golden-file equivalence tests: compare generated protos against reference outputs of configtxgen, cryptogen + configtxgen -printOrg, configtxlator compute_update, protolator, and the peer signtx flow using proto.Equal.",
    "Provide library APIs only (no end-user CLI); a thin test harness is built solely to drive integration tests against a local Fabric network so the orderer and peers validate generated transactions."
  ],
  "assumptions": [
    "A single senior Go developer (the author) performs all work, including design, implementation, testing and documentation; the developer is already familiar with Fabric internals.",
    "Baseline is Fabric release-2.x (2.0-2.3 era); supporting the 1.4 line beyond documentation references is out of scope.",
    "Cryptographic material for U3/U6 is provided as PEM-encoded X.509 certificates and ECDSA private keys; HSM/PKCS#11 support is out of scope for this increment.",
    "A prototypical configtx.yaml, MSP folders and sample network fixtures from the existing integration test suite are available as test fixtures.",
    "For U5 and U8, the caller supplies the current (base) channel configuration bytes; the library does not fetch configuration from a running network.",
    "U1 scope is limited to the default state database (LevelDB/CouchDB) and public read sets; private-data collection handling is only regression-tested, not redesigned.",
    "Estimates are effort in 8-hour focused workdays and include developer testing; they exclude dedicated QA/performance-test cycles, release management and ongoing maintenance.",
    "Asynchronous peer code review is available; expected review rework is included as a dedicated activity.",
    "A local Fabric test network (fabric-samples test network or equivalent) is available for integration and end-to-end verification."
  ],
  "activities": [
    {
      "activity_id": "A1",
      "activity_name": "Increment requirements analysis and solution architecture",
      "activity_description": "Analyze U1-U8, define the library API surface (CreateChannelTx, signing, assembly, compute-update, org/consortium builders), decide the U1 tamper-detection approach, and produce the overall design notes.",
      "most_likely_effort": 4
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A2",
      "activity_name": "Project and module setup",
      "activity_description": "Set up the Go module/repository structure, dependency pinning to the Fabric baseline, CI pipeline, linting, and test scaffolding including golden-file fixture management.",
      "most_likely_effort": 2
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A3",
      "activity_name": "U1 design: tamper-evident read set",
      "activity_description": "Design the read-set proto extension (value hash per read), channel-capability gating, new validation code, and backward-compatibility behavior; document the threat model from the referenced article.",
      "most_likely_effort": 2
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A4",
      "activity_name": "U1 implementation: proto and endorser changes",
      "activity_description": "Extend the rwset protobufs and simulator/endorser path so the endorsing peer records value hashes in the read set when the new capability is enabled.",
      "most_likely_effort": 3
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A5",
      "activity_name": "U1 implementation: validation changes",
      "activity_description": "Implement committer/VSCC validation that compares recorded value hashes against local world state and invalidates transactions on mismatch, wired into the existing state-based validation path.",
      "most_likely_effort": 4
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A6",
      "activity_name": "U1 unit tests",
      "activity_description": "Unit tests for endorser read-set population and validator comparison logic, covering tampered value, matching value, capability on/off, and missing-hash cases.",
      "most_likely_effort": 3
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A7",
      "activity_name": "U1 integration test on test network",
      "activity_description": "Integration test reproducing the referenced scenario: tamper a single endorsing peer's world state, submit a transaction, and verify other peers invalidate it instead of committing the tampered value.",
      "most_likely_effort": 3
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A8",
      "activity_name": "U2: copy and adapt genesisconfig data structures",
      "activity_description": "Copy Profile, Application, Orderer, Consortium, Consortiums, Capabilities and Policy types from genesisconfig into the new package, stripping viper/yaml coupling and adapting them to plain input data structures.",
      "most_likely_effort": 3
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A9",
      "activity_name": "U2: config group construction",
      "activity_description": "Implement builders that translate the adapted structures into channel-level ConfigGroup trees: application group, orderer group, consortiums map, capabilities and policies (implicit meta and signature policies).",
      "most_likely_effort": 4
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A10",
      "activity_name": "U2: MSP loading and organization embedding",
      "activity_description": "Load MSP definitions from an msp folder and embed organizations into the application/orderer groups so output matches configtxgen behavior for a prototypical configtx.yaml.",
      "most_likely_effort": 2
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A11",
      "activity_name": "U2: CreateChannelTx and genesis block assembly",
      "activity_description": "Implement CreateChannelTx with functional options, building the channel creation configuration envelope and the proto-encoded genesis block equivalent to configtxgen -channelID -profile output.",
      "most_likely_effort": 3
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A12",
      "activity_name": "U2: golden-file equivalence tests",
      "activity_description": "Generate reference blocks with configtxgen from the integration test suite's configtx.yaml and msp folder, and assert proto.Equal between those and the library output across representative profiles.",
      "most_likely_effort": 4
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A13",
      "activity_name": "U3: detached signature function",
      "activity_description": "Implement a function that takes a ConfigUpdate, channel ID and explicit key material (signing identity certificate and private key) and produces a detached ConfigSignature without consulting configuration for keys.",
      "most_likely_effort": 2
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A14",
      "activity_name": "U3: unit tests",
      "activity_description": "Unit tests verifying signature structure, creator identity serialization, and that produced signatures verify against the ConfigUpdate bytes.",
      "most_likely_effort": 1
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A15",
      "activity_name": "U4: assemble signed config update transaction",
      "activity_description": "Implement a function that combines a ConfigUpdate with a collection of detached signatures into a ConfigUpdateEnvelope wrapped in a signed common.Envelope acceptable to orderer and peer validation.",
      "most_likely_effort": 2
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A16",
      "activity_name": "U4: equivalence tests vs peer signtx flow",
      "activity_description": "Tests proving the assembled transaction is equivalent to one built by accumulating signatures with the existing peer signtx command, including ordering-independence of the signature collection.",
      "most_likely_effort": 2
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A17",
      "activity_name": "U5: max_message_count batch size update builder",
      "activity_description": "Implement a function that takes the current channel config and a new max_message_count value, applies the change to the orderer batch size, and returns an unsigned ConfigUpdate transaction (reusing the U7 compute-update logic).",
      "most_likely_effort": 2
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A18",
      "activity_name": "U5: tests vs manual configtxlator process",
      "activity_description": "Tests comparing the generated unsigned config update against one produced by the manual fetch/protolator/edit/compute_update flow, ignoring signatures applied by existing tools.",
      "most_likely_effort": 1
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A19",
      "activity_name": "U6: organization ConfigGroup generation",
      "activity_description": "Implement a function that builds an organization ConfigGroup (MSPConfig with root/intermediate/admin certs, OU identifiers, plus standard org policies and AnchorPeers value) directly from supplied cryptographic material, with no dependency on existing MSP material on disk.",
      "most_likely_effort": 3
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A20",
      "activity_name": "U6: equivalence tests vs cryptogen and configtxgen -printOrg",
      "activity_description": "Tests asserting semantic equivalence between the generated org ConfigGroup and the output of cryptogen plus configtxgen -printOrg for the same crypto material.",
      "most_likely_effort": 2
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A21",
      "activity_name": "U7: compute-update port",
      "activity_description": "Port configtxlator compute_update into the library: given only base and modified configs, build the read set and write set (groups, values, policies, mod policies) forming the ConfigUpdate message.",
      "most_likely_effort": 4
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A22",
      "activity_name": "U7: tests vs configtxlator compute_update",
      "activity_description": "Tests comparing library output with configtxlator compute_update over representative base/modified config pairs from the channel update tutorial scenarios.",
      "most_likely_effort": 2
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A23",
      "activity_name": "U8: add organization to consortium builder",
      "activity_description": "Implement a function that takes the system channel config, a consortium name and an org definition (reusing U6) and returns a signable channel update transaction adding the org to the named consortium (reusing U7).",
      "most_likely_effort": 2
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A24",
      "activity_name": "U8: tests vs documented manual process",
      "activity_description": "Tests comparing the generated update with the documented configtxgen -printOrg + protolator + configtxlator manual flow for adding an organization to a consortium in the system channel.",
      "most_likely_effort": 2
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A25",
      "activity_name": "End-to-end validation on a local Fabric network",
      "activity_description": "Stand up a local test network and verify orderer and peers accept and validate the generated channel creation, channel update, and consortium-update transactions end to end.",
      "most_likely_effort": 3
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A26",
      "activity_name": "Documentation",
      "activity_description": "Write package godoc, a README with usage examples for each user story (U2-U8), and short developer notes describing the U1 capability and validation behavior.",
      "most_likely_effort": 2
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A27",
      "activity_name": "Code review rework, refactoring and hardening",
      "activity_description": "Address review feedback, refactor shared internals (config group walking, policy construction), edge-case hardening and final cleanup before merge.",
      "most_likely_effort": 3
    }
  ],
  "reported_total": {
    "most_likely_effort": 70
  }
}

